# No border radius (hard rule)

This product uses **sharp corners only**. Border radius is not allowed anywhere in UI code or styles.

## Do not use

- Any Tailwind `rounded-*` utility except `rounded-none` (prefer omitting radius classes when `rounded-none` is redundant with global CSS).
- Inline `borderRadius` / `border-radius` unless setting `0`.
- Design tokens that imply curvature for UI surfaces (`--radius` is `0` in `packages/ui`).

## When editing UI

- Replace `rounded-md`, `rounded-lg`, `rounded-full`, `rounded-[…]`, etc. with square corners.
- Avatars, FABs, badges, charts, and calendar range pills follow the same rule (square, not circles).
- Do not introduce new rounded corners “just for polish.”

## Source of truth

Global enforcement lives in `packages/ui/src/styles/globals.css` (`--radius: 0` and base-layer `border-radius: 0`).
